## How this repo is built: an agent factory

Work happens through an issue-driven factory on Claude Code GitHub Actions. Agents write short designs, the maintainer signs off, then agents build, test and open PRs. Only the maintainer (@[[ maintainer_github ]]) can start or advance work, merge to `main`, or publish anything.

1. Open an issue with the **Factory task** template.
2. Add `factory:design`. The design agent writes `.factory/designs/issue-N.md` and opens a draft design PR.
3. Review it; iterate with `@claude …` comments or edit it yourself.
4. Add `design:approved` to the design PR. The build agent implements it on `factory/issue-N`, runs the checks until green and opens a PR.
5. The review agent checks the PR against the design and `CLAUDE.md`.
6. Merge. Releases stay manual.

| Label | Applied by | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `factory:design` | maintainer, on an issue | Ask an agent for a design |
| `factory:designing` | agent | Design in progress / awaiting review |
| `design:approved` | maintainer, on the design PR | Signed off: start building |
| `factory:building` | agent | Implementation in progress |
| `factory:review` | agent | Implementation PR open, awaiting merge |
| `factory:blocked` | agent | Agent hit something it shouldn't decide |

Agent rules live in [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md); the stage prompts in [`.claude/commands/`](.claude/commands/).

### Changing the factory itself

- **Workflow changes go in their own PR.** `claude-code-action` refuses to run from a workflow file that differs from `main`'s, so on a PR that edits `.github/workflows/factory-*.yml` the affected agent stage skips itself (the job still shows success). The change takes effect once merged. Don't bundle it with feature work.
- **After merging a workflow change, update open factory PRs before re-triggering them.** PR-triggered runs use the PR's merge commit, which GitHub doesn't rebuild when `main` moves, so an older design or implementation PR keeps running the old workflow. Click **Update branch** on the PR (or `gh api -X PUT repos/[[ maintainer_github ]]/[[ project_name ]]/pulls/N/update-branch`), then re-add the label or push.
- **Merging your own PRs:** GitHub never lets an author approve their own PR. Use the ruleset's admin bypass ("Merge without waiting for requirements to be met").
- **A run that ends without its artifact is a failure,** even if the job is green: a design run must open a draft PR, a build run an implementation PR, otherwise the agent must leave a comment and `factory:blocked`.

